think surveyed first — the design ground already stood: the Kumara Ledger Shape (active-reviving) reviving from the Azimuth-and-Sui study (external-research), five commitments and a translation table. Sui's gift is the object: a globally unique id, an owner, a version that climbs on every change; an address-owned object rides a fast path spending no global ordering on one owner's affairs
think chose the home — a new settlement/ dir, whitelisted in .gitignore beside kumara, with import symlinks mirroring comlink's pattern (topology.rye, kumara_tilak.rye, kumara.rye) so the module composes the geometry and the deed without copying them
think modeled a Settled point as the Sui object: both keys (identity signs turns, keeper owns and grants caps), sponsor, net key, two counters, and a version that climbs by exactly one per transition; the Constellation is a galaxy's d60 held in a bounded 66-slot array that never reallocates
think the transitions ARE the five commitments — open (genesis galaxy, its own bind the warrant), mint (a sow cap spawns a child under its rightful topology sponsor), transfer (a hand cap moves ownership), rotate (a tend cap sets a new signed turn while the keeper sits cold, a reset outranking a key bump)
think safety-first hardening — a public cap record alone must never authorize; the holder signs the specific act (child identity for mint, new keeper for transfer), verified under the cap's holder, closing the replay gap a bare cap would open
obs the first run went RED, correctly — I had transferred the planet before rotating, so the old keeper's tend cap was already void; the ledger refused it. reordered: rotate while the keeper still holds, transfer as the last act its caps authorize
obs the selftest proves the whole arc GREEN — genesis, two mints down the tiers, a transfer, a rotation with a keeper that never moves, a reset that outranks; and seven refusals: orphan parent, wrong sponsor, forged cap, forged spawn signature, a re-mint, a stale rotation, a turn signed by the wrong key
obs tame_style_check clean on constellation.rye (only the pre-existing REDS 64 python fossil flags); all five JARL witnesses run GREEN together — kumara_tilak, turn_route, handshake_turn, topology, settlement_constellation
